From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:51:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Document what /restart, /quit and /removegames do

The API summary at the top of HttpServerThread.cpp is the only reference
for the web API, and it lists these routes without saying what they do:

- /restart calls quitES(REBOOT), the same as RESTART SYSTEM in the quit
  menu, so it reboots the device. Scripts that want to restart only
  EmulationStation expect otherwise.
- /quit exits EmulationStation; Knulli's emulationstation-standalone loop
  then starts it again, so this is the route that restarts only ES.
- /removegames deletes each listed game file from disk, besides removing
  it from the gamelist.
---
 es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp b/es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp
index efa82a23..eb9990bc 100644
--- a/es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp
@@ -30,8 +30,8 @@
 Misc APIS
 -----------------
 GET  /caps                                                      -> capability info
-GET  /restart
-GET  /quit
+GET  /restart													-> reboots the system, like RESTART SYSTEM in the quit menu (not only EmulationStation)
+GET  /quit														-> exits EmulationStation; on Knulli, emulationstation-standalone starts it again
 GET  /emukill
 GET  /reloadgames
 POST /messagebox												-> body must contain the message text as text/plain
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ POST /systems/{systemName}/games/{gameId}/media/{mediaType}		-> body must contai
 Store APIs
 ----------
 POST /addgames/{systemName}										-> body must contain partial gamelist.xml file as application/xml
-POST /removegames/{systemName}									-> body must contains partial gamelist.xml file as application/xml
+POST /removegames/{systemName}									-> body must contains partial gamelist.xml file as application/xml. Deletes the listed game files from disk
 
 File APIs
 ---------
